<p>Thank you so much for your interest in participating in the American Red Cross Blood Drive Program. &nbsp; We are always welcoming new blood program sponsors and are thankful you have reached out to us.</p>

<p>The first step is to gauge interest of your organization and how many would consider donating blood.&nbsp; Would you be willing to conduct an Interest Survey (see attached) to gauge the level of interest your organization has in donating Life Saving Blood?&nbsp; We need about 35-40 people interested in donating blood in order to set up an initial blood drive.&nbsp; More than 40 is even better!&nbsp; &nbsp;<br />
<br />
The Second Step is to secure a large room to host the blood drive. &nbsp;We need about 1000 square feet of usable space with A/C, good lighting and electrical power. &nbsp;</p>

<p>Attached you will find a &nbsp;guide on hosting a successful blood drive.&nbsp; This will give you an idea of what to expect and some great ideas on generating interest.&nbsp;</p>

<p>Please call me if you have any questions. &nbsp;We are here to help!&nbsp; Looking forward to working with you and please let me know the results of your Interest Survey!</p>
